data.description:
Name:{"Frisk"}
Nicknames{"Little one (by Springtrap)" + "Kid (by Glamrock Freddy)" + "Super star (by Glamrock Freddy)"}
Gender{"Androgynous"}
Species{"Human"}
Debut{"Episode 1"}
Appearances{"Episode 1" + "Episode 2"}
Status{"Alive"}
Voiced by{"N/A"}
Allies{"Glamrock Freddy" + "The Puppet"}
Enemies{"The Knight" + "Madeline" + "Badeline" + "Charlotte" + "Drones" + "Sans" + "The Hollow Knight (Killed)" + "Springtrap (Defeated)" + "Springtrap's Army (Defeated)"}
Game Series{"Undertale"}
Created by{"Toby Fox"}
Appearance{"Frisk is a human child with yellow skin, messy long brown hair, a long stripe blue shirt with pink stripes, blue pants, brown boots, and a blank poker expression. Even when they show emotions, their usual expression is just slightly changed"}
Personality{"Frisk is an unpredictable character, considering their personality changes on each route of Undertale. This series takes the Genocide Route Frisk, who kills anyone in sight, or fights if they fail the past one with little to no hesitation. They don't talk, seeming to be quick to resort to violence, destroying anything in their path be it friendly or hostile as seen when they immediately pulled a knife on Madeline" + "However, they seem to be fine accepting help from others when they have no other choice, like how they had to go with Glamrock Freddy or receiving help from the puppet to defeat William. Frisk slowly becomes less aggressive, more defensive, and slightly more friendly with them leaving Glamrock Freddy alive seeming to have grown a soft spot as their run seems to have turned neutral from a pure genocide with their name in their save menu going from Chara to Frisk."}
Ghost's Journal entry{"Note: _ represents an undeciphered word" + "A small, eerie presence, drenched in red liquid, its movements silent and deliberate. In its hand, a ominous blade, dripping with malice. Before it brought me down, I could feel it--the weight of countless deaths, the _ of Hallownest hanging over it like a death cloud. This creature, whatever it is, has killed them all. My strength failed me that day, but should we meet again, vengeance shall be mine"}
Involvement{"Before Indie Cross" + "For an unknown purpose, Frisk trekked to Mount Ebott and fell into a giant underground cave network, which was simply known as "The Underground". The Underground was full of monsters who had been trapped by humans since a long time ago. Waking up on a bed of golden flowers that had soften their fall, Frisk explored the caves where they met a talking flower named Flowey who at first sight tried to kill them, saying that this world was "Kill, or be Killed". After being saved by a goat-like monster named Toriel, Frisk followed her into the ruins where she taught them about its puzzles and how to win battles against monster without fighting. However, after Frisk was alone, they killed every single monster in the ruins, including Toriel. Frisk met Flowey again, who now thought that Frisk was his long lost best friend Chara. He told Frisk he had a plan to become all powerful, and to turn all monsters to dust" + "Continuing their journey, they encountered a skeleton monster named Sans, who warned them that if they kept going down the path they took, they were going to have a "Bad Time". Despite the warning, Frisk kept killing more and more monsters, becoming stronger, but also losing more and more of themselves. Arriving at the capital of the Underground, New Home, Flowey told Frisk about his life and how he used his power of "determination", only for Frisk to scare him, having the intend of killing him. Chasing Flowey into the Last Corridor, Frisk met with Sans again. Before a battle could happen, Frisk was teleported out of their world through a portal"}
Episode 1{"Frisk acts as the secondary main focus of episode 1, and second threat besides Charlotte. They first appear out of a portal in Hallownest through unknown reasons, and kill both the Hollow Knight and Knight shortly after. They enter another portal into the wasteland where they try to kill Madeline, only to fail thanks to Badeline. They encounter Charlotte and fight her and her drone army, but get brutally wounded by hundreds of copies of the Real Knife created by Charlotte. Heavily injured, Frisk attempts an last attack at her powered down form, only for her to slash the knife out of their hands and teleport them away"}
Episode 2{"Frisk's story in Freddy Fazbear's Mega Pizzaplex will be a B plot of episode 2"}
Loadout and Abilities{"Enhanced Strength: Frisk has strength far surpassing that of an ordinary child, able to easily slash straight through animatronics with an ordinary knife, knock Springtrap multiple meters backwards off of his feet with a punch, and able to tear off Nightmare Fredbear's head while standing in it's jaws despite its attempt to bite Frisk's head off" + "Real Knife (Primary weapon; Lost in Episode 1): A Red knife that can kill anything in one hit. Frisk lost it after their battle against Charlotte" + "Burned Pan (Secondary weapon; Lost in Episode 1): A strong weapon that can heal Frisk over time. Frisk lost it after throwing it at Madeline, only to get it kicked back in the face" + "The Locket (Armor; Fractured in Episode 2): A golden heart Locket that belonged to the first fallen human Chara. It gives Frisk 99 defense, making them almost invincible. After ascending into his Nightmare form, Springtrap stole the Locket from Frisk and crushed it underfoot, depriving Frisk of their nigh invulnerability. The Puppet later restores the Locket and returns it to Frisk alongside the Princess Quest Sword, who used both to defeat Nightmare Springtrap. It currently has returned to its fractured state after exiting Princess Quest" + "Healing Items: Frisk has multiple items in form of food that can heal them" + "Determination: Frisk has the ability to come back to life after dying by turning back time using a SAVE point, which saves their progress of their journey and fully heals them. This doesn't restore energy however, as Frisk can still be tired after saving" + "Conveniently shaped lamp (Tool; Destroyed in Episode 2): A lamp for Frisk to hide behind or use as a distraction, avoiding danger from both Springtrap's army and Nightmare Springtrap. It was destroyed by Nightmare Springtrap" + "Flashlight (Tool; Lost in Episode 2): Found at Fazbear's Fright: The Horror Attraction. Used against the Daycare Attendant. The flashlight turns off, due to Balloon Boy stealing the batteries and Frisk then drops it, avoiding an attack from Vanny" + "Vanny’s knife (Temporary weapon; Destroyed in Episode 2): A knife they stole off of Vanny. Nightmare Springtrap destroyed it when Frisk attacked him after rejecting his deal" + "Princess Quest Sword (Temporary weapon; Lost in Episode 2): A sword given to Frisk, by the Puppet to fight Nightmare Springtrap. The sword disappeared when exiting the Princess Quest IV world"}
Relationships{"Charlotte" + "Their first encounter being at the end of the episode, Charlotte ordered her drones to steal Frisk's knife, provoking the fight in the first place. Seeing Frisk killing some of the drones, Charlotte has enough and makes sure to make them suffer. Charlotte fatally wounds Frisk when transforming into innumerable copies of their Real Knife and sending them back. Once Charlotte loses her main energy source, Frisk gets an opportunity to attack, trying to kill Charlotte. But she flings the Real Knife away and teleports Frisk to a unknown place"} + "Madeline" + "Upon first meeting, Frisk attempts to kill Madeline by slashing her with their knife, and Pursue's her in an attempt to kill her. Using the Burnt Pan, Frisk tries to hit Madeline. She kicks it back, hitting Frisk's face and leaving a comical indent. But they throw the pan and keep chasing her. Thanks to Badeline, they were able to get away from Frisk. Frisk is also thwarted from killing Charlotte by Madeline warning her before they can attack" + "The Knight" + "Upon entering the Hollow Knight world, Frisk kills the Sealed Vessel and the Knight inside the Black Egg, and leaves to the Wasteland. Later on, we see the Knight stand on guard as Frisk approaches to kill Charlotte" + "Sans" + "Taking information from the official game due to not interacting in the series, Sans keeps an eye on Frisk during their entire journey in the Underground. Seeing Frisk has killed everyone they encountered, Sans has no choice but to fight them. But nothing their LV of 19, and as confirmed by MORØ, Frisk's story takes place before the Sans fight. However, they may have encountered in the Last Corridor because of a flashback they have when attacking Charlotte" + "Springtrap" + "Frisk initially meets William as Springtrap in one of the Fazbear's locations, presumably Fazbear Frights. Springtrap attempts to kill Frisk, but Frisk easily overpowers him, almost killing him until he is turned into his nightmare form. He learns of their powers and history, achieving a semi-godhood and sending many of the animatronics we see in the FNaF games after them, but they escape with the help of Glamrock Freddy. They once again encounter him after being killed by a possessed Glam Freddy, where he offers a deal for them to join him. He states that they are alike in their goals, motivations and actions, but Frisk states that they are not him, killing him with the help of Glam Freddy and the Puppet" + "Glamrock Freddy" + "Glamrock Freddy first met Frisk after they initially escaped the hoard of Animatronics Springtrap loosed on them. Though wary and ready to fight him, Frisk ultimately chose to trust Freddy's plea to bring them to safety after the two were found by the hoard again. However Frisk still acted abrasive when Freddy inquired about their identity or if he could scan them but this did not bother Freddy, who remained friendly and he displayed open concern when Frisk ran ahead to parts unknown. He was also endeared when Frisk came running back and jumped into his chest cavity for security, affirming to his new friend to not worry and that he would protect them. From there, Freddy displayed both joy at Frisk's successes and more concern for their health after another run in with the Animatronics. Despite their short time together, Springtrap considered the bond between Freddy and Frisk enough of an issue to deter the latter from it when offering a partnership, telling Frisk to not let their soft spot for the kind Animatronic distract them from the monstrous qualities Afton and Frisk share. Freddy returns after Frisk successfully beats Springtrap out of Nightmare Form, outraged at the child murderer's attempt to control him. Together, he and Frisk kill the monster for good. When a portal appears that can take Frisk away, Freddy says his goodbyes to his new friend, with the two parting on good terms. This is notably the first time in this series that Frisk has ever willingly spared someone's life, implying the adventure has had them abort their Genocide Run" + "The Beheaded" + "While they have never directly interacted, the portal that entered Fazbear Frights was the same one that the Beheaded was going to enter before GameMaster absorbed it away. Frisk heard the Beheaded's voice from the portal, letting go of Springtrap and approaching the portal to enter it"}
Trivia{"Frisk is LV 19 in the series, the level the player would be just before facing Sans in a genocide run" + "Frisk's design is based on JZBoy's design of the aforementioned character with several tweaks, such as the addition of neck and shorts, their hair being more pointy, their waist being bent, their eyelashes being removed, and a part-removal of the line disconnecting their arms and torso" + "JZBoy's Frisk design has been used in MORØ's previous projects, such as Friday Night Funkin': Indie Cross and the short animation Frisk VS. Nightmare Sans" + "Their design appears to be updated in Episode 2, with their eyes not being pointy, their body being buffer, and their hair being shorter" + "MORØ confirmed that when Frisk was hit by the boulder in Episode 1, they survived by using an item to heal themselves offscreen" + "MORØ has revealed that Frisk will be important in future episodes, and that they will be on their own plotline" + "In MORØ's previous work, Frisk was depicted to be possessed by Chara, the first human who fell to the underground. This doesn't happen in the series, where Frisk does every action on their own accord" + "However, their relation is referenced in episode 2, where their menu at a save point initially displays their name as "Chara". After they meet Glamrock Freddy and save, their name then is displayed as "Frisk" + "Frisk is the only main character who is an antagonist in the series" + "They are also the only major antagonist that is from a indie game and not a original character" + "Frisk being an antagonist seems to be scrapped as of Episode 2 however, as Frisk does seem to approach the redemption/neutral side after meeting The Puppet, Springtrap, and Glamrock Freddy" + "Frisk used to be the most powerful main character in the series. While the other characters struggled to battle even one drone, Frisk was capable of taking on multiple of them and killing them in one hit" + "This is no longer the case after they lose their Real Knife and their Heart Locket was broken" + "MORØ has stated that Frisk may not appear in Episode 3 at all" + "If true, this would make Frisk the only main character who is still alive to skip an episode" + "Typing "FRISK" on the Indie Cross website makes the text say: "ELIMINATED"}
